{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794877280204705745,"compiled_state":{"alias":"waxy-nonspheral-cutworm","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8b9b5f38e425d86fc054e24382c298f009772d660bc878481be8967b32f8e9fa","event_uuid":"821855f0-dd9b-4d03-af57-24dee85b3105","position":{"commit_sha":"b882d6c42f1026fb6654a0081aa209a15c7b3396","position":"1794877266519759800-821855f0-dd9b-4d03-af57-24dee85b3105"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7227932845b992f7f1697c1758494b6b0470de5f642328c77b5d6c6ef3aa7bd2","event_uuid":"9fde1f4e-a035-4d6e-bf43-7403df43f35f","position":{"commit_sha":"a3dc0a9eebaf6d732d4fb6eb1d10cc8dd6970603","position":"1794877280204705744-9fde1f4e-a035-4d6e-bf43-7403df43f35f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1794877266519759800,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9fde1f4e-a035-4d6e-bf43-7403df43f35f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e152-4009-4180-4fd8"}],"description":"## Observation\n\n- In the MCP base image (`python:3.12-slim`), running `rebar.llm.completion.verify_completion` repeatedly in one process with no model credentials grew `sys.getallocatedblocks()` by about 115k per run (788,561 -> 904,180 -> 1,019,794). Of that growth, 18,437 objects per run were `OrderedDict`s whose keys were `type/members/document/documentation`, which matches botocore service-model shapes. Python-level RSS rose about 8-9 MB per run.\n- On the live container `rebar-mcp-9beecb409abb-8093` (with the malloc_trim fix 9beecb409ab), idle anonymous memory after 3 plan-review gates was 328 MB, against 230 MB at fresh start. glibc thread arenas held only 21 MB of that; the remaining ~98 MB sits in other anonymous memory (Python objects). `malloc_trim` cannot release live objects.\n\n## Not established\n\n- Whether the growth is unbounded per run (a leak) or levels off after a few runs (a cache). The local run covered only 3 iterations, and the model turn did not run.\n- What keeps the objects alive: a per-run boto3 session/client that something retains, or botocore's loader caching per new session.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The owner of the retained per-run objects is identified with evidence (a referrer chain from a retained botocore object to a module-level or long-lived object).\n- [ ] Either the per-run growth is removed or shown to level off, measured with at least 10 gate runs in one process.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mcp"],"ticket_id":"e266-c398-f5cd-4a3c","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Each MCP gate run leaves about 100k Python objects (botocore service-model data) alive after it finishes","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["821855f0-dd9b-4d03-af57-24dee85b3105","9fde1f4e-a035-4d6e-bf43-7403df43f35f"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794877280204705745,"uuid":"cc5ae3f6-70c5-4a87-a92f-37e9a4270630"}